        <aside class="container ps-3 pt-3 py-5">
            <details open>
                <summary >
                    <h2 class="text-uppercase fs-5">
                        glosario tecnico<i class="bi bi-arrow-right-short"></i>
                    </h2>
                </summary>
                    <table class="table table-bordered table-striped table-hover">
                            <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Words</th>
                                <th>Meaning</th>
                                <th>Words</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Hue</td>
                                <td>The pure color itself, such as red, blue, or yellow, before any white, black, or grey is added.</td>
                                <td>El color puro en sí mismo (azul, rojo, amarillo).</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Palette</td>
                                <td>The specific range of colors chosen by a designer to be used together in a collection.</td>
                                <td>El conjunto de colores seleccionados para una colección.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Shade</td>
                                <td>A darker version of a color created by adding black to the original hue.</td>
                                <td>Un color al que se le ha añadido negro para hacerlo más oscuro.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Contrast</td>
                                <td>The visual difference between two things, such as light and dark colors, which helps elements stand out.</td>
                                <td>Diferencia notable entre dos colores opuestos.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Trend</td>
                                <td>A popular style, color, or look that is widely adopted by people during a certain period.</td>
                                <td>Lo que está de moda en un momento específico.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Monochromatic</td>
                                <td>A design style that uses only one color, but in different variations, tones, or shades.</td>
                                <td>Diseños basados en un solo color con diferentes intensidades.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Textile</td>
                                <td>A type of cloth or woven fabric, such as cotton, silk, or wool, used to create garments.</td>
                                <td>La tela o material del que está hecha la ropa.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Runway</td>
                                <td>The long, narrow platform where models walk to display new clothing collections to an audience.</td>
                                <td>El lugar donde se presentan las colecciones de moda.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Sustainability</td>
                                <td>The long, narrow platform where models walk to display new clothing collections to an audience.</td>
                                <td>Crear moda sin dañar el medio ambiente.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Fit</td>
                                <td>The way a piece of clothing fits or sits on a person’s body (e.g., loose, tight, or tailored).</td>
                                <td>Cómo queda la ropa en el cuerpo de una persona.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Complementary</td>
                                <td>Colors that are located directly opposite each other on the color wheel; they create high contrast and look bold together.</td>
                                <td>Colores que están opuestos en la rueda y resaltan entre sí.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Fast Fashion</td>
                                <td>A business model that produces large amounts of inexpensive clothing very quickly to keep up with changing trends.</td>
                                <td>Producción masiva de ropa económica que cambia constantemente.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Silhouette</td>
                                <td>The overall shape or outline created by a piece of clothing when worn on the body.</td>
                                <td>La forma general que crea una prenda sobre el cuerpo.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Collection</td>
                                <td>A series of new designs or garments presented by a designer, usually centered around a specific theme.</td>
                                <td>Un grupo de diseños presentados bajo un mismo concepto.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Vibrant</td>
                                <td>A term used to describe colors that are very bright, intense, and full of life.</td>
                                <td>Colores que se ven muy vivos, intensos y brillantes.</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
            </details>
